1. Chicago has the highest median nightly price at $235.50, meaning a typical listing in Chicago costs more per night than in Columbus or the Twin Cities.
2. The Twin Cities has the highest average rating at 4.82, indicating that listings in the Twin Cities receive the strongest average guest ratings of the three cities.
3. Columbus has the highest percentage of entire-home listings at 82.6%, meaning most listings in Columbus offer the entire home or apartment rather than a private or shared room.
4. The Twin Cities has the highest percentage of listings accommodating six or more people at 42.33%, indicating that it has the largest share of listings suited for larger groups.
5. Chicago has the highest median reviews per month at 1.73, meaning the typical Chicago listing receives about 1.73 reviews per month.